==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Croco]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*1 [[Berserkory]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Cala Maria]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Berserkory]] spawns.
**Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 46.67~50 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,500f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Kang Roo]]s spawn, delay 70~73.33 seconds<sup>2,100f~2,200f</sup>.
**1 [[Kang Roo]] spawns.
**1 [[Kory]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Though this stage may seem daunting at first glance due to the combination of Kory + Berserkory + Cala Maria, it is not that difficult with the right units.

[[Octopus Cat]] is highly recommended, as its Wave Shield ability coupled with its low recharge time allow you to replace it rather easily. though this does require at least four meatshields so that Cala Maria doesn't kill your Octopus. One recommended meatshield to bring is [[Ramen Cat]] due to his resistance to Angels: At a high enough level, he can tank a hit from Cala Maria and/or a hit or two from Berserkory. When paired with Octopus Cat, [[Courier Cat]] can be used to chip down Berserkory very well.

Almost any [[:Category:Cats with Wave Immunity|Wave-immune unit]] is welcome here, as they can help chip down both Kory and Berserkory even in case of Octopus loss. Some examples include [[Talents|Talented]] [[Li'l Mohawk Cat]], who can keep the meatshield line relatively stable; Talented [[Dancer Cat]], who can stay back at a safe distance from both Kory and Berserkory; or [[Miyamoku Musashi (Special Cat)|Heroic Musashi]], who can bring down a decently powerful attack from afar every once in a while.

Once you have gotten rid of Berserkory, the other enemies' pushing power is greatly reduced. Kory should be much easier to face due to his lack of Area Attack as well as a drastically reduced [[Wave Attack|Wave]] size compared to his [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] counterpart, and, once he too is dead, Cala Maria doesn't stand much of a chance on her own.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Machine Mk 3]]: Its resistance to Red enemies coupled with Wave Shield allow it to act as a wall for Berserkory, making it much easier to stack up your units and dispose of him before Cat Machine dies.
*[[Momotaro (Uber Rare Cat)|The Peach Devils]]: While they aren't immune to Waves without an Ultra Talent, they can still provide great support as getting off a freeze could buy your stack valuable time in chipping off either Berserkory or Cala Maria.

==Trivia==
*Steamed to Death's Japanese name, Yukemuri Gokuraku Jigoku (湯けむり極楽地獄, "Hot Spring Smoke Paradise Hell"), hints at the presence of [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]] in the stage. The word ''gokuraku'' (極楽) means "paradise", "heaven", or the Buddhist concept of a [[wikipedia:Pure land|pure land]].

